-- title:
--   Centre of the Gauss valuation is minimal over varpi
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $p$ and whose image in $L$ contains $\zeta$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$, let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $j \in K$, $j \neq 0$, have underlying Laurent series the image of $\mathrm{jq} = q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the } j\text{-numerator power series})$ under the coefficient map. Further data: a natural number $d$ coprime to $Mp$, an $L$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $K$ which, for elements with equal underlying Laurent series, agrees with the base change to $L$ of the diamond automorphism $\langle d\rangle$ of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$; and a ring endomorphism $\rho$ of the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ (the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$) inducing $\theta$ on $K$. Finally let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ with the Gauss description: $f \in W_0$ iff there are $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a minimal prime $\mathfrak{P}_1$ of the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ such that, for every $s$ in this chart algebra, $s \in \mathfrak{P}_1$ if and only if $s$, viewed in $K$, is a non-unit of $W_0$. The diamond data $d$, $\theta$, $\rho$ occur only as hypotheses; they do not appear in the conclusion.
--
--   This identifies the centre of the Gauss valuation on the $j$-finite chart of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ as a height-one prime, namely a minimal prime over the uniformiser, cut out by the non-units of $W_0$. It is used in showing that the diamond operator $\langle d \rangle$ fixes this prime on the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_mem_minimalPrimes_span_forall_mem_iff_coe_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_chartAlgFin_x1_mul.lean

